  "question": {
    "text": "The eye can be regarded as a single refracting surface. The radius of curvature of this surface is equal to that of the cornea <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>.8</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi>mm</mi><mo>)</mo></math>. This surface separates two media of refractive indices <math><mn>1</mn></math> and <math><mn>1.34</mn></math>. Calculate the distance from the refracting surface at which a parallel beam of light will come to focus.",
